    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n49796" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἰβύ</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>loudly</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Phot.
			</span></i>: hence aor. 1
			inf.
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἰβυκινῆσαι</span></b> ,
			<i>shout</i>, Telecl<i><span class="en">
				Id.
				58
			</span></i> (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἰβυκηνίσαι</span></b> 
			<i><span class="en">
				<u>EM</u>
				464.44
			</span></i>): but Subst.
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἰβυκανητής</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οῦ</span>, ὁ,= <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βυκανητής</span>, <i>trumpeter</i>, read by <i><span class="en">
				Suid.
			</span></i> in <i><span class="en">
				Plb.
				2.29.6
			</span></i> (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βυκανητῶν, βυκανιτῶν</span>
			codd.). 
				Ion.
			 words, acc. to <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i>: derived from the poet Ibycus, <i><span class="en">
				Suid.
			</span></i></div>
